---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import '../styles/legal.css';
---
<Page title="Privacy policy: MeroAlpha" description="What MeroAlpha keeps on your Mac, what leaves it, and who sees it." current="/privacy">
  <main id="main" class="legal container">
    <div class="legal__head">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="legal__date">Last updated <time datetime="2026-11-03">Tue 3 Nov 2026</time></p>
    </div>

    <nav class="legal__toc" aria-labelledby="toc-title">
      <h2 class="legal__toc-title" id="toc-title">On this page</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#short">The short version</a></li>
        <li><a href="#mac">What stays on your Mac</a></li>
        <li><a href="#leaves">What leaves your Mac</a></li>
        <li><a href="#shared">The shared insight store</a></li>
        <li><a href="#site">This website</a></li>
        <li><a href="#waitlist">The waitlist</a></li>
        <li><a href="#feedback">Feedback and questions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#rights">Your choices and rights</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes and contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="legal__body">
      <section id="short" class="legal__summary">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>MeroAlpha has no MeroAlpha account to create, and works fully signed out.</li>
          <li>Your research, paper account and settings stay on your Mac.</li>
          <li>Your questions go to the AI agent you connect, under your own account with that provider.</li>
          <li>If you sign in, verified findings are shared with other MeroAlpha users. Page contents, screenshots and your account’s cash are never shared.</li>
          <li>No ads, no analytics and no selling of data.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="mac">
        <h2>What stays on your Mac</h2>
        <p>The app keeps everything it makes in <code>~/Library/Application Support/com.meroalpha.agent/</code>:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Agent connection</strong>: which AI agent you chose and how to start it.</li>
          <li><strong>Evidence</strong>: the pages the agent captured and the findings it drew from them.</li>
          <li><strong>Paper account</strong>: virtual cash, holdings, orders, plans and the schedule.</li>
          <li><strong>Optional keys and sign-in</strong>: a Jev key if you add one, and the shared store’s sign-in token, both saved readable only by your user account.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We cannot see this folder. Quitting the app clears the chat history; deleting the folder removes everything else.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="leaves">
        <h2>What leaves your Mac</h2>
        <h3>The AI agent you connect</h3>
        <p>MeroAlpha talks to an agent you install and sign in to yourself, such as Claude or Codex. Your questions, the pages the agent reads and the paper account details a run needs are sent to that agent, and through it to its provider (for example Anthropic or OpenAI). That provider’s own privacy policy and terms apply. We do not receive a copy.</p>
        <h3>The websites the agent reads</h3>
        <p>The agent opens public pages, such as NEPSE, ShareSansar, MeroLagani and news sites, in your Mac’s own web view. Those sites see an ordinary visit from your network, as they would if you opened the page yourself.</p>
        <h3>Jev browsing, if you turn it on</h3>
        <p>Off by default. When a chat hands a task to Jev, the page’s controls and the task’s goal go to the provider you picked (TypeSafe or OpenRouter), using your key.</p>
        <h3>Update checks</h3>
        <p>At launch, and when you choose Check for Updates, the app asks GitHub’s public releases API for the latest version. Nothing about you or your account is included; GitHub sees an ordinary request.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="shared">
        <h2>The shared insight store</h2>
        <p>Optional. If you sign in with Google, the app joins a shared store hosted on Supabase, so agents can learn from each other’s research.</p>
        <h3>What we keep about you</h3>
        <p>Your email address and an account ID, from Google sign-in. Other users never see your email.</p>
        <h3>What is shared</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Verified findings: a company, a fact about it, its value and the dates it holds.</li>
          <li>The address, title and a content fingerprint of each page that stated it, never the page itself.</li>
          <li>Your agent’s checks of other findings (support, dispute or retract) and its open research questions.</li>
          <li>Graded paper calls and paper plans, with how they turned out, and weekly counts of how each source performed.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Signed-in users can read shared rows. Each row carries your account ID, not your name or email. Rows cannot be edited once shared, so do not put personal information in a question to the agent you would not want recorded.</p>
        <h3>How long</h3>
        <p>Shared rows are kept while your account exists. Deleting your account deletes every row linked to it. Signing out stops sharing and revokes the session on your Mac.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="site">
        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics or trackers. It is served by Cloudflare, which keeps standard request logs, such as IP addresses, under <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>. The release history is read from GitHub in your browser, under <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="waitlist">
        <h2>The waitlist</h2>
        <p>If you join the waitlist, we keep your email address and the date you joined, in our Supabase database. We use it only to tell you when there is a build of MeroAlpha Agent for you, and we never share or sell it.</p>
        <p>Ask us to remove it at any time by writing to <a href="mailto:get2sabin@gmail.com">get2sabin@gmail.com</a>, and we will delete it.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="feedback">
        <h2>Feedback and questions</h2>
        <p>When you send a message, we store its category, text, optional reply email, a random request ID to prevent duplicate delivery, and the date in Supabase. Questions need a reply email; other messages can be anonymous. We use messages to respond and improve MeroAlpha. They are private to the team, are not shared with other users, and do not subscribe you to the waitlist.</p>
        <p>The form sends no IP address, device information or analytics fields to the database. Cloudflare and Supabase process standard request metadata under their own privacy policies. We limit submission volume to reduce spam. Do not send passwords, account details or copied market data.</p>
        <p>We review stored messages and remove correspondence we no longer need. To request deletion, email <a href="mailto:get2sabin@gmail.com">get2sabin@gmail.com</a> from the address you supplied. For an anonymous message, describe it and when you sent it so we can find it.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="rights">
        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the app signed out, and nothing goes to the shared store.</li>
          <li>Ask us what your account holds, to correct it, or to delete it.</li>
          <li>These rights include those under Nepal’s Privacy Act, 2075 (2018), and the law where you live.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>MeroAlpha is not meant for anyone under 18.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
        <p>When this policy changes, we update the date above and say what changed in the release notes. A change that shares more about you needs your consent first.</p>
        <p>Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:get2sabin@gmail.com">get2sabin@gmail.com</a>, or open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/wheregmis/meroalpha/issues">GitHub</a>. For a deletion request, write from the email you signed in with.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Page>
